      "lineNbr": 34,
      "author": {
        "id": 7953
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-11T11:33:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "https://www.w3.org/TR/webgpu/#texture-view-creation\nBased on the spec, the wgpu::Texture can not be sampled or rendered directly. A wgpu::TextureView has to be created from wgpu::Texture::CreateView(). A texture view just offers us a view into the texture. The texture view is not like GL framebufer object. It can be used as both render target and a static texture. Just because we can not get texture from swapchain, so we need this ctor.\n\nFor the ctor BackendTexture(wgpu::Texture texture), the BackendTexture will hold the texture. When the backend is used, we still need to create a texture view from it with the default properties.\n\nAnd if I read the spec correctly, I think we can read or write pixels data to a wgpu::Texture directly, but wgpu::TextureView doesn\u0027t support them. But I think skia can draw pixels to the wgpu::TextureView instead of copy, and can draw wgpu::TextureView to another intermedia texture and then copy pixels from it. So I feel all skia API can works with both texture and texture view.",
      "parentUuid": "58cf6858_7acd7ace",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 34,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "fb31ab7cf4fddbcc9b395f7d945d9680087039bb",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
